{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed","id":888039,"title":"Roleplaying the Lupus Breed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-11T04:17:01-07:00","id":888039,"title":"Roleplaying the Lupus Breed","content":"Imagine taking someone from a small tribal village somewhere, and plonking them down in central London. They would be completely lost - for a start, they wouldn't know the language. They wouldn't know the culture, the traditions, the ways of interacting; they'd probably barely know the technology. If they walked into a bar, they wouldn't know what one does in a bar, how one does it, how one interacts with anyone there - they wouldn't even know what a bar was. Thousands of rules of behaviour - like where to defecate, how to dress, and how/when to kiss people - would be completely unknown to them (the same is true in the other direction, of course, but I'm focusing on the tribal fish out of water in London for a reason).<br /> <br /> However, most tribal people today, except the most extremely isolated, have some idea of things like technology, and the sheer scale of the human planet in terms of inhabitants. If we take someone from a tribe from another time in history, their alienation would be even greater; they might not have any idea of what these flashing lights are, or that so many people could ever exist.<br /> <br /> Now imagine that you start with a new species...<br /> <br /> This is what it's like being a lupus breed werewolf in homid form. You may have the cognitive capacity to be human, but remember that you can't speak the language, don't know how to wear clothes, have no idea of human hygiene, table manners, and social interactions (but very clear ideas on lupin-appropriate ones), and have never dealt with more than at most ten individuals at once.<br /> <br /> It takes years for humans to learn all these skills, and we start early. So interactions between homid lupus breeds and normal human should remain a baffling and alien experience (on both sides) for many years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 05-11-2016, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:42:00-07:00","id":888051,"title":"","content":"Mhmm, given that Werewolfs in WtA are half wolf, half human, half spirit (I know, I know it's &quot;part....&quot;) I don't think they would be that far off being human. Surely in the beginning there would be some problems but that evens out after a while. Maybe they don't get proverbs and the like and take things quite literally but I don't think they should be to estranged from their human side. Same as homid shouldn't be to estranged from their wolf side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T05:00:02-07:00","id":888069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meldok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=888051#post888051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mhmm, given that Werewolfs in WtA are half wolf, half human, half spirit (I know, I know it's &quot;part....&quot;) I don't think they would be that far off being human. Surely in the beginning there would be some problems but that evens out after a while. Maybe they don't get proverbs and the like and take things quite literally but I don't think they should be to estranged from their human side. Same as homid shouldn't be to estranged from their wolf side.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, let's start simple: how and when are they going to learn the local language? *Humans* from other cultures and times would be estranged from modern westernised humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:01:15-07:00","id":888095,"title":"","content":"That's why Lupus generally avoid entering cities. Also they speak Garou Tongue so they can learn monkey talk at their own pace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:34:32-07:00","id":888118,"title":"","content":"Had one player once in a game on aol who INSISTED on playing her char as an athiest, and interjecting all kinds of political bullshit, like revering humans as &quot;Superior predators&quot; sneering at environmentalism, etc... she left in a huff when i didnt start creating other loonys for her to make friends with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:15:37-07:00","id":888157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=888069#post888069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, let's start simple: how and when are they going to learn the local language? *Humans* from other cultures and times would be estranged from modern westernised humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 changed things so that they still start with a human language. So that's no longer an obstacle, at least. Otherwise, it's kind of like being Inuyasha when he visits Kagome in the present time. Misunderstandings abound, and unfortunately for most lupus, they aren't the wacky romantic comedy kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:23:07-07:00","id":888164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=888069#post888069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, let's start simple: how and when are they going to learn the local language? *Humans* from other cultures and times would be estranged from modern westernised humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's turn the argument around. How does a homid learn the wolf side? Because this gives renown subtraction if you ignore it to long. So how do they learn that? So I would argue that you learn that from a lupus in your sept. So the lupi learn the homid stuff from other homids. If you are a youngling without guidance I would agree with you put since every wolf has a pack they keep care of at least the basic stuff which should include some survival training in the city for a lupus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:28:01-07:00","id":888169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meldok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=888164#post888164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's turn the argument around. How does a homid learn the wolf side? Because this gives renown subtraction if you ignore it to long. So how do they learn that? So I would argue that you learn that from a lupus in your sept. So the lupi learn the homid stuff from other homids. If you are a youngling without guidance I would agree with you put since every wolf has a pack they keep care of at least the basic stuff which should include some survival training in the city for a lupus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homid cubs generally adjust to it quickly, but otherwise have to spend time buying up Primal-Urge. They immediately learn how to communicate, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:40:08-07:00","id":888187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=888169#post888169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Homid cubs generally adjust to it quickly, but otherwise have to spend time buying up Primal-Urge. They immediately learn how to communicate, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Still they have to learn it and a homid cub from a big city adjusted to the city life style has the same problem learning to get one with nature, primal urge, hunting prey, etc. He may never really understand it at all but the cub will learn at least the basics with some misconceptions but nothing to huge normally. And I argue it would be the same the other way around with a lupus cup, he might never get a PhD in ancient Greek literature but he will get the important basics in time with a few misconceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:24:57-07:00","id":888279,"title":"","content":"While I think there's a bit of over-thinking going on for a game...<br /> <br /> I feel like canids are being a bit underestimated here. Wolves are extremely intelligent, and like most non-human mammals, incredibly fast learners. Wolves go from helpless pup to fully productive member of their pack in ~2 years. And that's not just instinct. There's a huge amount of learned behavior that goes into their lives.<br /> <br /> Something I love to paraphrase: humans are so smart as a species, because we're actually all really dumb by animal standards. Most social animals learn extremely complex things magnitudes faster than humans do, with better reaction times, and better memory; they also tend to be far better independent learners that can learn simply by watching and doing themselves rather than needing to be taught. We take absolutely forever to learn things. We suck at figuring things out without someone else teaching us over and over.<br /> <br /> We win the &quot;smart&quot; race though, because our extremely slow-ass brains force us to think harder and longer on things, and our reliance of education makes us better at large social organization.<br /> <br /> So yes, a Lupus should experience some culture shock after their first change and their subsequent learning about how to fake being human. However they're exceedingly better wired to adapting to that situation than any normal human would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:41:43-07:00","id":888359,"title":"","content":"One thing I've always pondered, is how long it would take a homid cub to understand wolf behaviour. iven how much the whole dominance-based thinking for wolves and other canids is still seen as a fact (i.e that there is an alpha among real wolves), how many homid cubs have gotten a bad rep by the lupus/wolf-kin for acting like douchebags XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:30:59-07:00","id":888515,"title":"","content":"Like most things, learning is complicated.<br /> <br /> How long would it take a homid to learn how to &quot;wolf&quot; enough to at least not look like an idiot? How were they raised? A Glasswalker who's closest exposure to wolves is their neighbor's dog is going to have a much steeper learning curve than a Silver Fang who works at the family wolf sanctuary front for maintaining high breeding lupus-kin lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T18:55:12-07:00","id":888746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=888069#post888069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, let's start simple: how and when are they going to learn the local language?</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems hard because we know in real life, learning a language takes many years of constant exposure. But for the game, I don't think it is an issue. The quickness and ease at learning the local language is probably covered by the &quot;part spirit&quot; stuff. This is a game after all where a single Gift allows you to talk to spirits (Spirit Speech), to all animals (Beast Speech), and any human language of the area you just showed up in (Assimilation). Knowing the local human language is probably an innate power/gift provided by the collective Ancestor spirits of the Garou or as a gift from Gaia or Luna.<br /> <br /> But you just get the one. If you want anything more, you have to figure it out. If there are multiple languages spoken in the area that are equally dominant, then in-character it's probably innately known as well, although out-of-character mechanically you need to buy it with Freebies.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the Garou isn't immediately fluent with it. It's probably like when people grow up speaking a language, and then move far away and never speak it again. They seem to forget it. But once they return home, it quickly comes back and you speak it near fluently after a couple of months. I imagine that is how it is like for lupus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T19:10:22-07:00","id":888752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed#post888039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what it's like being a lupus breed werewolf in homid form. You may have the cognitive capacity to be human, but remember that you can't speak the language, don't know how to wear clothes, have no idea of human hygiene, table manners, and social interactions (but very clear ideas on lupin-appropriate ones), and have never dealt with more than at most ten individuals at once.<br /> <br /> It takes years for humans to learn all these skills, and we start early. So interactions between homid lupus breeds and normal human should remain a baffling and alien experience (on both sides) for many years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homid Garou need to learn &quot;Primal Urge&quot; to master things, but they still know the basics of how to act like a wolf. I imagine for a certain but more limited extent, it is the same for lupus to understand humans. Luna has &quot;cheated&quot; a bit so that knowing how to be the other species is not a complete blank slate once the First Change happens.<br /> <br /> Some of it may come in the form of Ancestor spirits. Some of it may come in the form of Mentors teaching them as cubs, and utilizing gifts like Dreamspeak, Shadows by the Firelight, of Gift of Dreams. Some of it may even come in the form of &quot;instinct&quot; provided by Gnosis - and lupus start with a lot of Gnosis.<br /> <br /> There is also the issue that the young always seem to learn faster than older people because they have no preconceptions. Give a child and an adult an iPad, neither of whom has experienced with one before, and more than likely the child has figured it out far faster than the adult.<br /> <br /> There may be a whole series of &quot;rank zero gifts&quot; given to cubs (meaning spirit teachers allied to the Garou) that zap them with certain basic knowledge about how to be a Garou that tells them not only basics of the other species, but also things unique to being a Garou like the speaking the Garou Tongue, how to develop your Gnosis or increase Rage, being able to consistently move across the Gauntlet, etc.<br /> <br /> In any event, the lupus has to be able to master the basics in the time allotted to be a cub. Depending on who you talk to, this period is either several months or several years.<br /> <br /> You are bringing up a valid point, but I think you can justify a wide variety in how well lupus can understand human society. A Red Talon likely is still very unsettled and ignorant about many things, while a Glass Walker lupus probably understands many things &quot;rationally&quot; but is still inexperienced.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T21:00:14-07:00","id":888816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed#post888039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine taking someone from a small tribal village somewhere, and plonking them down in central London. They would be completely lost - for a start, they wouldn't know the language. They wouldn't know the culture, the traditions, the ways of interacting; they'd probably barely know the technology. If they walked into a bar, they wouldn't know what one does in a bar, how one does it, how one interacts with anyone there - they wouldn't even know what a bar was. Thousands of rules of behaviour - like where to defecate, how to dress, and how/when to kiss people - would be completely unknown to them (the same is true in the other direction, of course, but I'm focusing on the tribal fish out of water in London for a reason).<br /> <br /> ..snip..<br /> <br /> It takes years for humans to learn all these skills, and we start early. So interactions between homid lupus breeds and normal human should remain a baffling and alien experience (on both sides) for many years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points all. Though i do feel Lupas kin would get trained ON those factors as needed BY their homid brethren, well unless they were red talons!!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=888279#post888279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I think there's a bit of over-thinking going on for a game...<br /> <br /> I feel like canids are being a bit underestimated here. Wolves are extremely intelligent, and like most non-human mammals, incredibly fast learners. Wolves go from helpless pup to fully productive member of their pack in ~2 years. And that's not just instinct. There's a huge amount of learned behavior that goes into their lives.<br /> <br /> Something I love to paraphrase: humans are so smart as a species, because we're actually all really dumb by animal standards. Most social animals learn extremely complex things magnitudes faster than humans do, with better reaction times, and better memory; they also tend to be far better independent learners that can learn simply by watching and doing themselves rather than needing to be taught. We take absolutely forever to learn things. We suck at figuring things out without someone else teaching us over and over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice angle Heavy. Also, a lot of humans just can't seem to grasp some stuff without book learning it, while others pick up better via On the Job training, and yet others still learn best from repitition from an instructor. Compare that to all animals, and only the latter 2 are there for them to learn from, and for most its a very quick pick up rate...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T23:38:22-07:00","id":888892,"title":"","content":"Well, what makes humans special in that regard, is that we care about &quot;why.&quot; But why takes a ton of brain power, and slows down learning. Regardless of how an individual leans best, we learn fastest when we know why what we're learning is important (it makes it easier for us to encode learning in long term memory when we can associate it with something important to us already).<br /> <br /> An example from primate studies: Once you show most apes to tap 1 through 10 in order on a touch screen for a reward, they pick it up very quickly. Humans can, of course, do the basic task very quickly as well. It's when you start making it harder you see massive performance differences. Like if you scramble the numbers around the screen, or you only flash the numbers for a second, the other apes will perform pretty much as fast as if the numbers are just listed in order normally. Humans start struggling (many can't successfully pass the &quot;flash for a moment&quot; test).<br /> <br /> The apes have zero brain power invested in what each of those symbols mean beyond &quot;what order to press them in to get the reward.&quot; To us, each of those numbers registers a huge amount of associations &quot;1&quot; means more than just &quot;the symbol you press before 2&quot; and that stops us from being able process the input quickly.<br /> <br /> But all those associations are what lets us be &quot;smart&quot; because those associations allow us to handle abstract thoughts. We care about &quot;why&quot; 1 comes before 2, and what that means on a larger scale. That's pretty much our entire evolutionary strategy that lets us purposefully invent tools. In the wild we've observed chimpanzees using all sorts of tools, but there seems to be very little experimentation. They seem to only discover improvements by accident. We cared about &quot;why&quot; the sharp stick is better for stabbing prey, which meant we can associate &quot;sharpness&quot; in the abstract with other things, like rocks, to make stone spears. That's the connection that other animals don't make, that made it worth it for our brains to be so large, and so invested in very very slow learning patterns in comparison.<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> Getting back to wolves and learning: Wolves understand the concept of verbal communication; they have a fairly complex verbal system for coordinating while hunting. It's why dogs can take to verbal commands; they're wired to want sound-based communication as part of socialization. Lupus would actually have very little problem understanding lots of human things. Toilets for example, are no mystery to them. Wolves (like most small and medium non-apex predators) don't like feces building up around their dens because (especially if it's pup feces) it can attract larger predators. The idea of &quot;making it go away&quot; is completely sensible to a wolf (even if the whole flushing thing is a big &quot;why&quot; they wouldn't quite get, but they wouldn't really care either).<br /> <br /> The thing that probably frustrates Homids and Metis trying to teach Lupus is that the Lupus are used to learning direct things. &quot;When someone holds out their hand like this, shake it firmly,&quot; is all the Lupus probably cares about, but Homids esp are going to be used to explaining the whole social aspect of it being a form of greeting, and getting into what different ways of doing it &quot;mean&quot; and such that to the Lupus is actually frustrating information overload.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:06:17-07:00","id":889247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=888752#post888752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There may be a whole series of &quot;rank zero gifts&quot; given to cubs (meaning spirit teachers allied to the Garou) that zap them with certain basic knowledge about how to be a Garou that tells them not only basics of the other species, but also things unique to being a Garou like the speaking the Garou Tongue, how to develop your Gnosis or increase Rage, being able to consistently move across the Gauntlet, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this way of looking at things. That would be a cool reason to get cubs into the Umbra earlier, as long as they could get something out of it without needing Spirit Speech. Run with a spirit pack and the spirits all around you help you figure out what you're doing. Not even a hundredth the level of the Assimilation gift or anything, but enough that like...balancing when you run on all fours makes more sense, or the very concept of human-language grammar feels more intuitive. It makes &quot;how to human / wolf&quot; training feel more like an extended training montage instead of a years-long slog, at least to the point where you can run a Rite of Passage campaign without the lupus philodox sounding like a kindergartner every time she tries to be diplomatic with humans. It doesn't have to be a lifelong boon, could even just last long enough to learn your first language...but that definitely seems like the kind of thing the Garou would have made a pact with their spirit allies for a long, long time ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:06:58-07:00","id":889346,"title":"","content":"I think playing a lupus well, while tricky, is easier than people think. Likewise, playing homid well is much harder than most players perceive at first. Warning: this is going to be a long post.<br /> <br /> Having a shared language in the garou tongue makes the transition much easier, I imagine. If the newly changed lupus can communicate with other garou right off the bat, they can start learning pretty quickly. Sure, its going to take a while to learn a lot of things, but I imagine a lot of septs are also experienced with teaching new lupus and kind of have their own systems for it down pretty well. Plus, having more experienced lupus teach lupus cubs probably eases that transition a lot, as the older lupus has a better idea of what is going to be harder to learn, how to explain it in ways lupus would understand, and prioritizing what cubs need to learn based on their own experiences.<br /> <br /> But there is a lot more to this issue, too. The first is that, well... garou are made for this shit. They are designed to be able to perform their functions, and part of their function is to deal with humans. Garou &quot;instincts&quot; go beyond primal urge, or connecting to gnosis, or being able to cross the gauntlet - all of which, in my opinion, <i>any</i> garou could and probably would pick up over time even without training. Their job and duties, the things they were designed to do, are as much as part of who they are as anything else. The spirit part of them isn't passive, its active, and imbues them with a sense of purpose that will urge them towards the functions they are meant to perform, because it is in a sense part of <i>divine plan</i>. That's how I see it; maybe others don't, and that's fine. But I do think a lot of people underestimate this aspect.<br /> <br /> Then you have the fact that not only are wolves more intelligent than most humans give them credit for, lupus aren't normal wolves. The game explicitly describes that lupus are exceptionally smart and their intelligence sets them apart from there kinfolk pack, to the point where they can even kind of recognize that they are different. Now, that intelligence and sentience doesn't reach &quot;human&quot; levels until the first change, but they are already more primed for it. Their &quot;brain&quot; isn't as undeveloped and immature as a human baby, for example. The garou brain is also really weird to talk about, because how do garou brains even work when they can shift size and shape and capabilities? That literal and metaphorical malleability no doubt allows them to form new neural connections way faster than normal. Think about THAT.<br /> <br /> On top of this, not all lupus are completely new to garou. There are much fewer wolves left in the wild in modern times - though it is variable just how many you want there to be. In some ways, that makes it way easier for garou to keep track of them, not to mention literally being able to track them via their own senses, records, and spirits (or even human technology... ew). Garou may come around a specific wolf packs fairly often. A pre-change lupus might even have exposure to more organized sept life. They can no doubt sense that garou are somehow related to them and aren't human; garou certainly smell differently, they can interact with wolves in different forms to make them more comfortable, and (should) know the wolf body language and vocalizations. Not to mention animal ken and beast speech. I'm playing a lupus character in a game right now who grew up in a group of protected kinfolk wolves that were within the territory of a sept. It's entirely reasonable for a pre-change lupus to wander closer and closer to the sept, drawn by curiosity and even other garou, and may even grown comfortable there. Once there, a pre-change lupus would start picking up patterns and various aspects of more &quot;human&quot; interaction. Hell, dogs can learn human body language and tone - a lupus would probably pick up quite a bit, even if they didn't have the means to piece it together and understand the meaning behind the patterns they observe.<br /> <br /> But seriously though, beast speech. Garou can outright talk to pre-change lupus. Not the same as more advanced communication, and the lupus won't learn nearly as much as they will post-change, but still.<br /> <br /> Lupus might be 14 or so human years of learning behind, but it could be as few as 10. An early change lupus will have a decent amount of time to learn, and their minds are ready for it. Abstract concepts and cultural knowledge will take them longer, but they don't really need <i>that</i> much to get by. So much of what we learn is unnecessary. It's all about priorities. And, a lupus will mostly likely never be able to completely blend in outside of the sept, and probably will not want (or need) to be the one handling subtle interactions with humans. But remember, that's already a bitch and a half for garou at all, because of <b>the curse</b>. Werewolves stick out most of the time whether they want to or not, and <i>not</i> in a good way. People will be suspicious of them. People will be afraid of them. People will read them as aggressive and intimidating for no reason. And most humans will react to the curse by just avoiding them completely if possible. A weird, poorly socialized (for human standards) lupus garou in the city is probably not going to have to deal with many human interactions unless they specifically need to. It just won't be that easy for them, and therefore probably won't be that important. Let the homid handle the yakety yak.<br /> <br /> Right now I'm playing my fostern-rank lupus philadox as pretty much competent as far as the english language and being able to not act particularly weird around humans. His vocabulary isn't awesome, and he doesn't get most cultural references. A lot of homid/human humor is lost on him. The smells and sounds of the city are still awful, but he's been there long enough that he's desensitized to it quite a bit. He enjoys human food, and having thumbs. He doesn't get style on his own, but he can emulate it by observing people and ads and magazines etc.... because he's smart. Really smart. No academics, no formal education, missing a lot of context, but very sharp, and he <i>watches</i> and <i>listens</i> (and often smells things/people, often inappropriately). His eye for body language (esp. with Heightened Senses) mean he's <i>really</i> good at telling when people are lying, or afraid, or aggressive, etc, which give him a lot of context in conversations. He's a philadox, so judgment and negotiation and arbitration are part of his purpose, and he has the mind for it. Learning the various cultural meanings behind things is a matter of exposure, but discerning details, complex patterns, and emulating behavior don't require full understanding - and he absorbs as much cultural information as he can along the way. TV and internet make this even easier, if you aren't opposed to using it. He can learn a ton about various human cultures with a couple of hours of that a day. Seriously, the way mass communications have revolutionized learning and cultural exposure is immense, and there's no reason garou can't incorporate it into their lupus teaching regimens, even if they do so very selectively.<br /> <br /> To give some last thoughts: Lupus <i>are</i> part human, arguably just as much as homid; they lack experience, but it is an essential part of who they are that can't be denied any more than a homid can deny they are wolf (yeah, shut up Red Talons). While human civilization and technology has grown more complex, in some ways modern culture is more homogeneous and approachable. Humanity has way more shared experiences, language, and culture than ever before, so gaining a working knowledge of human culture might be easier now, because you can go to way more places and the same knowledge set will be useful. Garou have the means and motivation to track kinfolk wolf populations very closely and interact with lupus even before their first change. They have systems and practices (and even technology) for teaching lupus that have been refined and improved over millenia. Lupus minds are primed for learning not just through highly enhanced intelligence but through spiritual design and guidance. Their senses and instincts can actually help them navigate human social environments, as humans are still animals. Most garou don't live in cities, most septs are not in areas of high human population, and if defending Gaia is your purpose... well, a majority of the earth's surface is not yet inhabited by humans. Plus you know, the umbra. Lupus are difficult to play well, but they are not as foreign and hard to play as many players I know make them out to be. They seem intimidating to many because wolves are so different. But Lupus are not wolves, they are garou. Playing a lupus well shouldn't necessarily be harder than playing a homid well; homid players often downplay things like primal urge, rage, the curse, the difficulties of embracing their wolf aspects, as well as connecting with nature. Hell, most animals and spirits are going to be way more suspicious of you if they recognize you as homid rather than lupus. And lets not forget <b>gnosis</b> - the disparity in starting gnosis by breed is pretty damn big, and that <i>isn't just mechanical</i>! Coming into their full heritage as garou should be baffling for many years for pretty much any character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3533-sonofgaia","name":"SonOfGaia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T18:36:11-07:00","id":889528,"title":"","content":"Minor nitpick: You mean sapient, not sentient. Sapience is &quot;thinking&quot; (aka why we call ourselves <i>Homo sapiens</i>), where sentience is an &quot;awareness&quot; and the ability to recognize oneself as a unique individual . Almost all social mammals (and probably a lot more) are provably sentient. Sapience is a very vague concept that's harder to nail down - and then prove exists - just like intelligence; but in general use the level of complex and abstract reasoning a pre-change Lupus is capable of is going to be above average for a wolf, but far below any changed Garou.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, awesome post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:30:08-07:00","id":889661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=889528#post889528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor nitpick: You mean sapient, not sentient. Sapience is &quot;thinking&quot; (aka why we call ourselves <i>Homo sapiens</i>), where sentience is an &quot;awareness&quot; and the ability to recognize oneself as a unique individual</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick of the nitpick: sentience is the capacity to feel pain and discomfort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T00:05:00-07:00","id":889713,"title":"","content":"Erm, no. That's a specialized application regarding animal rights (the idea that sentient organisms like other animals suffer emotionally from pain, unlike say plants, and thus should be treated humanely). The philosophic concept of sentience refers to the ability to feel anything subjectively; rather than just reacting to a stimulus. Sentient and non-sentient organisms all respond to stimuli. Pain is one of those responses. Things like dread, joy, and anxiety are signs of sentience. The thing about those emotions is that they require an awareness of the context of the stimulus inspiring them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T06:30:10-07:00","id":889839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SonOfGaia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=889346#post889346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now I'm playing my fostern-rank lupus philadox as pretty much competent as far as the english language and being able to not act particularly weird around humans. His vocabulary isn't awesome, and he doesn't get most cultural references. A lot of homid/human humor is lost on him. The smells and sounds of the city are still awful, but he's been there long enough that he's desensitized to it quite a bit. He enjoys human food, and having thumbs. He doesn't get style on his own, but he can emulate it by observing people and ads and magazines etc.... because he's smart. Really smart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thumbs are great. The other characters in my game kept threatening to take Renown from my Lupus Wendigo Ahroun for learning Firearms, but hew ass an <i>Ahroun</i> and <i>killing people</i> was his frickin' job. They also thought he was very easy going because he never reacted to the Fianna Philodox's spewing invective and bizarre sense of humor, never truly getting that, as a Lupus, he didn't <i>care</i> about her stupid jokes enough to even think about what they could possibly have meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T08:00:29-07:00","id":889897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=889839#post889839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thumbs are great. The other characters in my game kept threatening to take Renown from my Lupus Wendigo Ahroun for learning Firearms, but hew ass an <i>Ahroun</i> and <i>killing people</i> was his frickin' job. They also thought he was very easy going because he never reacted to the Fianna Philodox's spewing invective and bizarre sense of humor, never truly getting that, as a Lupus, he didn't <i>care</i> about her stupid jokes enough to even think about what they could possibly have meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the revised Glass Walker tribebook noted, <i>Klaives</i> are technology. A lupus is going to, like all garou, use what they have to fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T08:52:22-07:00","id":889947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=889713#post889713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm, no. That's a specialized application regarding animal rights</div> </div> </div> </div>Ethics as they pertain to the policy and management factors of research, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T08:53:57-07:00","id":889949,"title":"","content":"It's still not the totality of the philosophic concept of sentience...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T00:02:01-07:00","id":890466,"title":"","content":"If we're allowing the &quot;spirit&quot; aspect of the Garou to bridge the two cultures, this should also work between human cultures. There's nothing special about current western culture that makes it easy to understand for outsiders; rather the reverse, in fact. So Garou must be ultimately adaptable, adjusting easily to the many traditional tribal cultures, Aztec culture, Tibetan monastic culture, Pharaonic Egyptian culture, every era of Japanese culture, etc...<br /> <br /> In this view, would most field anthropologists be Garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T11:47:19-07:00","id":890683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=890466#post890466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're allowing the &quot;spirit&quot; aspect of the Garou to bridge the two cultures, this should also work between human cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are gifts that do that like Speech of the World and Assimilation, but they are more powerful than what cubs have access to. Such knowledge is also not permanent, lasting a scene or so.<br /> <br /> However, I would not use &quot;culture&quot; as the word to describe the difference between humans and wolves. Luna blessed all the Changing Breeds to cross between humanity and the animal world. Her blessings/gifts obviously must somehow allow that. She didn't give any blessings or gifts to bridge the divide between human cultures.<br /> <br /> There is magical thinking involved here, so you can't be strictly rational. Luna and Gaia had very specific goals in mind when they created the Changing Breeds. You can't force that to go into another direction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T07:12:20-07:00","id":898887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=890466#post890466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're allowing the &amp;quot;spirit&amp;quot; aspect of the Garou to bridge the two cultures, this should also work between human cultures. There's nothing special about current western culture that makes it easy to understand for outsiders; rather the reverse, in fact. So Garou must be ultimately adaptable, adjusting easily to the many traditional tribal cultures, Aztec culture, Tibetan monastic culture, Pharaonic Egyptian culture, every era of Japanese culture, etc...<br /> <br /> In this view, would most field anthropologists be Garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing how as a majority of tribes come from the mindset of conquering other cultures I guess you could say they adapt quite well, after the initial period of burning, looting and subjugating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:47:36-07:00","id":900082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Ways-Wolf-Sourcebook-Werewolf-Apocalypse/dp/1565040449\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Ways-Wolf-Sourcebook-Werewolf-Apocalypse/dp/1565040449\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Ways-Wolf-Sourcebook-Werewolf-Apocalypse/dp/1565040449\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.amazon.com/Ways-Wolf-Sourcebook-Werewolf-Apocalypse/dp/1565040449 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2385/Ways-of-the-Wolf?it=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/2385.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2385/Ways-of-the-Wolf?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> Ways of the Wolf - White Wolf | Werewolf: The Apocalypse 1st Edition | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2385/Ways-of-the-Wolf?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2385/Ways-of-the-Wolf?it=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Ways of the Wolf - The Midnight Prowl Dark shapes lope across the moon-drenched fields, hard upon the scent of prey - wolves on the hunt. T </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The best book I got for role playing wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:06:50-07:00","id":900150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=900082#post900082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Ways-Wolf-Sourcebook-Werewolf-Apocalypse/dp/1565040449\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.amazon.com/Ways-Wolf-Sour.../dp/1565040449</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2385/Ways-of-the-Wolf?it=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/2385.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2385/Ways-of-the-Wolf?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> Ways of the Wolf - White Wolf | Werewolf: The Apocalypse 1st Edition | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2385/Ways-of-the-Wolf?it=1\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2385/Ways-of-the-Wolf?it=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Ways of the Wolf - The Midnight Prowl Dark shapes lope across the moon-drenched fields, hard upon the scent of prey - wolves on the hunt. T </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The best book I got for role playing wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, while it has a lot of good points, it is outdated in how wolves are actually understood these days. No alphas or omegas, just parents and kids.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T22:01:43-07:00","id":900686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=900150#post900150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, while it has a lot of good points, it is outdated in how wolves are actually understood these days. No alphas or omegas, just parents and kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rightly or wrongly, the Alpha dynamic is built into Werewolf the Apocalypse, and similar hierarchies could easily be justified among the relatively intelligent Lupus kinfolk. We aren't talking about real wolves, we are talking about approximating pretend ones that sometimes turn into monsters or people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T23:08:09-07:00","id":900718,"title":"","content":"Also, a lot of the outdated concepts of wolf social structures are applicable to the Garou. The problem with how people originally constructed their ideas of how pack dynamics work was based around a bunch of wolves in captivity that didn't have the continuity of family of wild packs. Which is the essential dynamic of Garou packs. Garou packs aren't a mated pair and a few generations of off-spring that haven't set off to start new packs, they're a bunch of Garou from different backgrounds forced together.<br /> <br /> The dominance hierarchy dynamics that are built into WtA actually make sense from the context of why they're wrong about wild wolves being exactly why they're right for the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T04:44:26-07:00","id":900828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=900686#post900686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rightly or wrongly, the Alpha dynamic is built into Werewolf the Apocalypse, and similar hierarchies could easily be justified among the relatively intelligent Lupus kinfolk. We aren't talking about real wolves, we are talking about approximating pretend ones that sometimes turn into monsters or people.</div> </div> </div> </div>The alpha dynamic works perfectly with garou. As Heavy Arms before me said, the issue is that people view actual wolves like that.<br /> <br /> Heck, even WtA writers know this. Tribebook Shadow Lords revised has a whole page on differences between actual wolves and alpha-dynamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T17:05:32-07:00","id":902375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=900718#post900718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dominance hierarchy dynamics that are built into WtA actually make sense from the context of why they're wrong about wild wolves being exactly why they're right for the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The hierarchy reported on wolf packs initially worked because scientists were interpreting packs of wolves not related to each other (because they were studying artificial wolf packs created by captured animals) and not natural wolf packs in the wild formed from family dynamics.<br /> <br /> However, Garou are not family members, but unrelated people working together, so the artificial pack structure originally studied should make sense for them.<br /> <br /> Of course, the human/primate inheritance of Garou should also be found. Even lupus Garou aren't really wolves because they too have a human side. Humans and primates have a hierarchical society as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:03:25-07:00","id":904159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/888039-roleplaying-the-lupus-breed?p=900150#post900150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, while it has a lot of good points, it is outdated in how wolves are actually understood these days. No alphas or omegas, just parents and kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I got it real cheap myself thanks to a going moving sale. Still a good source for some aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}